<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Cifra calls shareholders meeting.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Cifra calls shareholders meeting.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican store chain Cifra SA said Tuesday that it had called an extraordinary shareholders meeting and annual general meeting for June 24 to approve the recently-announced merger with Wal-Mart Stores Inc.</p>
<p>In information sent to the Mexican Stock Exchange, Cifra said it will propose a one-time dividend payment of 0.75 peso per 3,200,000,000 outstanding shares at the meeting. The dividend is part of the merger move.</p>
<p>Cifra and Wal-Mart announced June 3 the merging of their joint venture companies and that Wal-Mart planned to eventually take a 50 percent controlling interest in the Mexican store chain.</p>
<p>((--Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289562))</p>
